WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.560
Hey, good afternoon, dear people.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.300
Here I am today with a new video.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:16.900
Yesterday I was talking with my clients about whether they prefer to read texts, watch recordings or listen.

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:28.180
And I really got the impression that people like to put earphones in their ears and listen to smart things, smart people.

5
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:35.900
So, well, I get really good feedback from you on these short YouTube videos.

6
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:45.640
I find it interesting because this way I can say much more than I could write in that Instagram format.

7
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.680
Although I am someone who loves interactive work.

8
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:56.020
So I still haven't gotten used to recording something on camera and talking, right?

9
00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:06.300
But I have a lot to say, and I truly feel sorry for all of it to stay in my head or in my office between me and a client.

10
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:17.340
I truly want to reach more of you, so that you can play any video at any moment when you need it.

11
00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:26.960
And I always hope that any video can brighten your day, get you moving, lead you to some idea.

12
00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.410
For you to think about yourselves, to get moving, to do anything at all.

13
00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:36.770
For that video of mine to push you into some action.

14
00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:40.220
That is my idea, that is my intention.

15
00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:49.160
And I think that if I managed to get one person moving today, yesterday and tomorrow, that is an unprecedented success for me.

16
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.600
Now, what did I want to tell you today and what did I want to talk about?

17
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.150
About anxiety.

18
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.140
Why about anxiety?

19
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:10.680
I could record a video about it every single day, for the simple reason that anxiety has been over-represented in the last two years, let's say.

20
00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:36.550
And I think there is no day in my office when an anxious client has not walked in, whether in the form of a panic attack or some other form, in the form of ordinary unease, nervousness, tension, whether it is about some phobias or more serious anxiety states, such as OCD and so on.

21
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:41.980
But every day I get the chance to talk with anxious people.

22
00:02:42.100 --> 00:03:00.140
And what is very important for me to tell you, given my experience with people who come in and are anxious: they are of course very frightened, they have real sensations of fear, bodily sensations of fear, and they come for help.

23
00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:08.840
In fact, for someone to give them the information that nothing will happen to them and what is actually going on with them.

24
00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:26.140
My experience says that in this fast time we live in, when the healthcare sector is overloaded, doctors, experts and professionals do not have much time to deal with people, which is of course devastating.

25
00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:41.090
On the one hand, on the other hand, there are probably few professionals for the number of people who need them, so, say, a visit to a psychiatrist lasts five or ten minutes, which is unacceptable.

26
00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:56.740
And of course the person is in even greater panic about what is happening to him: he got some therapy, got something to calm him down, one pill in the morning and one in the evening, and he has no idea what is happening to him.

27
00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:13.800
And believe me, people, sometimes one good educational format, session or one video on the subject of what anxiety is can help much more than any pill.

28
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:27.070
So what I have noticed in my practice is that sometimes it happens, as Irvin Yalom would say, that we finish the whole psychotherapy in one meeting.

29
00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:45.640
That is, the person came only for information about what is going on with them, and when you explain it well enough and educate them well enough, they really leave much relieved, and that anxiety drops and decreases a lot.

30
00:04:45.640 --> 00:05:04.980
So I think there is nothing more important than education, especially if you perceive that this education, information and knowledge is given to you by a person whom you value as worthy, as high-quality and who can give you good information.

31
00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:21.840
That is of course very significant, so I hope the information you hear from me today will be significant and valuable enough for you, so that you can grasp what anxiety is and what it is all about.

32
00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:45.240
Many psychological theories, many books and much similar terminology have really been written about anxiety, but I like most to explain it in a way that you understand very simply, so that you can of course apply it in your life and in the way that will serve you best.

33
00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.420
So, anxiety, my dear people, is not an illness.

34
00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.950
That is the first thing you must grasp.

35
00:05:50.950 --> 00:06:11.480
Although in some classifications we can put it under some F codes, some numbers and so on, what is important is that you know anxiety is not an illness, that you are not sick, that you are not some psychiatric cases, that you do not have to go to hospital treatment, for anything.

36
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:22.900
Especially cardiovascular diseases, especially neurological wards — there is nothing people do not do when they are in a state of anxiety.

37
00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:29.840
Very often they come to me with huge folders of examinations by various specialists.

38
00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:35.200
It is important that you know it is absolutely not a physical illness.

39
00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:55.180
It has been scientifically proven that you cannot die from anxiety, nothing can happen to you, you cannot get a heart attack, you cannot even get a stroke, very rarely you can faint, and above all you cannot go crazy.

40
00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.050
So these are scientific facts.

41
00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.680
It absolutely cannot happen.

42
00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:11.790
Even though your bodily sensations are truly frightening, because it is a really genuine, authentic emotion of fear.

43
00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:20.980
Fear is an evolutionary emotion and without fear I do not know how long we would survive at all on this planet Earth.

44
00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:42.400
But there is an important difference between neurotic fear, which is what anxiety is, and real, objective fear, when we are in real mortal danger, such as, I don't know, you are sitting on a plane and the plane is falling, so of course you will have a bodily sensation of fear.

45
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:52.400
Certain chemical processes are secreted in the body and then you naturally feel frightened because of real danger to life.

46
00:07:52.400 --> 00:08:20.060
But anxiety is neurotic fear, that is, invented in our heads, because we judge that certain bodily sensations threaten our life and our brain perceives that we are in real danger, which of course we are not, because we imagined it with our imagining, our thinking, our fantasy.

47
00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:39.460
For example, if you are afraid and thinking how your heartbeat is going faster, faster, faster, faster, you have made a whole circus in your head that says: aha, now I will get a heart attack, when will I get a heart attack, will I collapse, will I die.

48
00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:54.320
And that goes on in an endless vicious circle, from which it is hard for you to get out unless you educate yourself about what anxiety is and that in fact nothing can happen to you from anxiety.

49
00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:59.080
The main point on the subject of anxiety is: there is no running away from it.

50
00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:09.360
So, my dear people, every time you run away from anxiety, it gets entrenched, concreted, becomes even stronger, and next time even stronger and stronger.

51
00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.320
Instead, we face it.

52
00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:22.860
So we can finish a panic attack, and anxiety too, in two sessions, in three sessions, if people understand this well and we make a plan and a program.

53
00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:40.120
In one session we will learn which beliefs are the problem, in the second session we will face, expose ourselves to our fear, to potentially frightening situations such as shopping malls, elevators, cars.

54
00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:51.420
And in the third session we already have a huge drop in anxiety on a scale from 1 to 10, where 10 is the highest anxiety: we are already at a two.

55
00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:55.960
So, what did I want to tell you today with this video?

56
00:09:55.960 --> 00:10:05.680
My dear people, well, I am watching, these minutes and seconds are ticking away, and so as not to drag it out, I could talk for three hours.

57
00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:27.840
The two most important things you must remember on the subject of anxiety are: anxiety is not an illness, it is a state we enter through our way of thinking, and the second important thing is that nobody in this world has come to harm from anxiety.

58
00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:36.270
So nobody has died, nobody got any illness, and anxiety is not life-threatening.

59
00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:56.120
This is important to understand and know, and if you persist in facing your anxiety, you can truly learn to live with it in a way that each time you know how to control it and each time you know what it is about.

60
00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:03.690
And when you learn that, there will be fewer and fewer situations when anxiety appears at all.

61
00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:12.510
So it is very important to educate yourself and very important to know that anxiety happens to everyone, including you.

62
00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:17.940
So nothing terrible or awful, you just need to know how to deal with it.

63
00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:23.900
Well, goodbye, dear people, enjoy your day, I love you and send kisses to all.

64
00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:24.260
Ciao!
